title: Social Security
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/dhss.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and social_security_timer <= 0
on-arrival: social_security_timer = 5; month_actions += 1

= Social Security

The Department of Health and Social Security spends a quarter of all public money, most of it on pensions. With unemployment [? if unemployment < 8 : rising ?][? if unemployment >= 8 : at [+ unemployment_2 +]% ?], the bill for benefits grows every month.

- @pension_link: Break the link between pensions and earnings.
- @benefit_cuts: Tax benefits and abolish the earnings-related supplement.
- @sick_pay: Make employers pay sick pay.
- @child_benefit: Raise child benefit.
- @fraud: Crack down on benefit fraud.
- @fowler: Introduce Fowler's reform of social security.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@pension_link
view-if: pension_link_broken = 0
subtitle: +1 budget now, and a growing saving every year. Pensioners will notice in time.
on-arrival: pension_link_broken = 1; budget += 1; de_con -= 2; c1_con -= 1; wet_dissent += 4; dry_dissent -= 3
achievement: pension_link

Until now the state pension has risen each year with prices or earnings, whichever was higher. From now on it rises with prices alone. The saving is small this year and enormous in twenty. Barbara Castle, who created the link, calls it theft from the old.

@benefit_cuts
view-if: benefits_cut = 0
subtitle: +1 budget, and benefit costs a fifth less from now on. Requires a dry Social Services Secretary.
choose-if: health_dry = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ health_secretary +] won't cut benefits in a recession.
on-arrival: benefits_cut = 1; budget += 1; de_con -= 2; de_lab += 1; c2_con -= 1; wet_dissent += 3; dry_dissent -= 2

Unemployment and sickness benefit become taxable, and the earnings-related supplement paid in the first six months out of work is abolished. Someone who loses a skilled job now falls straight onto the basic rate.

@sick_pay
view-if: sick_pay_reform = 0
subtitle: +0.5 budget. Small businesses grumble.
on-arrival: sick_pay_reform = 1; budget += 0.5; ab_con -= 1; dry_dissent -= 1

Employers will pay the first eight weeks of sick pay and reclaim it from their National Insurance contributions. The DHSS saves money and staff; the Federation of Small Businesses complains about paperwork.

@child_benefit
subtitle: -1 budget. Families and the wets approve.
on-arrival: child_benefit += 1; budget -= 1; c2_con += 2*(1-dissent); de_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 3; dry_dissent += 2

Child benefit rises faster than prices. It goes to the mother, and most mothers notice.

@fraud
view-if: fraud_drive < 2
subtitle: +0.5 budget. Popular with the tabloids; the Liberals object to the methods.
on-arrival: fraud_drive += 1; budget += 0.5; right_dissent -= 2; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); de_con -= 1; lib_relation -= 2

Specialist claims teams descend on benefit offices in search of "scroungers". In Oxford, a raid arrests 283 people at a fake benefit office the police set up to catch them. The Sun is delighted.

@fowler
view-if: second_term = 1 and bill_fowler = 0 and fowler_reform = 0 and time >= bill_fowler_wait
subtitle: +1.5 budget, once it becomes law. The poverty lobby and the wets will fight it.
choose-if: bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ bill_room_text +]
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 3; dry_dissent -= 2; bill_new = "fowler"
call: bill_introduce

[+ health_secretary +] publishes the Social Security Bill, the result of the biggest review of the welfare state since the war.
